    "title": "Reverse an expected development",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-reversal-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Reverse an expected development",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Reject the expected development, then state a contrasting actual result. The reversal must connect to the expectation rather than merely add a fact. 不是…吗 introduces an expectation; 还/还是 then marks an outcome contrary to it. 还是 can stress that the expected change did not occur.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他不但没生气，反而笑了。",
                "pinyin": "tā bùdàn méi shēngqì ， fǎn'ér xiào le 。",
                "meaning": "He was not angry; on the contrary, he laughed.",
                "audio": "d3b161341a9cb03623ea9f419689f0dfe46f9279be05d95a68a99bb521d7303f"
              },
              {
                "text": "你不是说不来吗，怎么还来了？",
                "pinyin": "nǐ bù shì shuō bù lái ma ， zěnme hái lái le ？",
                "meaning": "Did you not say you were not coming? Why have you come anyway?",
                "audio": "f8da4a23d624d3c859165ed0262fa89a34a24127ab9db65a6e99f46eef58e2db"
              },
              {
                "text": "不是已经解释了吗，他怎么还是不明白？",
                "pinyin": "bù shì yǐjīng jiěshì le ma ， tā zěnme háishi bù míngbai ？",
                "meaning": "Was it not already explained? Why does he still not understand?",
                "audio": "6480f9cef2d7d855690854dc959bbbee9c50d330f24ee67dbed5fbb61a3c8c73"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
